## Output handling

- Default output is JSON (parseable). Pipe through `jq` for queries.
- `--agent` turns on JSON + `--compact` + `--no-color` in one flag.
- `--format json|jsonl|csv|plain|pretty` picks a different shape; `--select id,name` keeps only the fields you need.
- Add `--pretty` for human-readable output.
- Add `--no-cache` to bypass the local SQLite mirror, `--dry-run` to see the request without sending it.

## Failure modes

HTTP errors are emitted as `{"error": ..., "status": ..., "body": ...}` on stderr,
with a typed exit code to branch on:

| exit | meaning |
|---|---|
| 0 | success |
| 3 | 404 not found |
| 4 | 401/403 — auth missing or rejected (check the env vars above) |
| 5 | other API error |
| 7 | 429 rate limited — back off and retry |
| 10 | local configuration error (no base URL, no such profile) |

Run `{{ cli_bin }} auth-doctor --probe` to find out whether credentials are actually accepted.
